For the federal paper, the census frame of twelve appropriations bills per year from 1975 to 2024 (600 episodes), approximately eighty debt-ceiling episodes, and approximately sixty statutory-expiration episodes, with a source file name and missingness rate for each. For the state paper, the LegiScan coverage audit for all fifty states, the Squire professionalism scores from the 1979–2021 update , and the Klarner margin variation . The audit produces a 2 \times 2 selection table crossing high versus low professionalism with commission versus legislative redistricting. If the audit yields fewer than twelve chambers with continuous coverage, the paper reports the actual number and reframes the design as a comparative case study.

